1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,118
In March 2026, Reddit was cited in about one in five US ChatGPT answers. By September, it was closer to two in a hundred.

2
00:00:11,317 --> 00:00:18,931
So if your plan to get cited by ChatGPT is copied from last year's advice, it may be out of date.

3
00:00:19,131 --> 00:00:26,457
In the next five minutes: how to read ChatGPT's sources list, and turn it into a short action plan.

4
00:00:26,657 --> 00:00:33,119
First, two different wins. Mentioned means your brand name appears in the answer.

5
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:40,405
Cited means a page is listed as a source. Your own page, or a page about you.

6
00:00:40,606 --> 00:00:47,571
For most brands, the goal is to be mentioned. The sources list shows you the route there.

7
00:00:47,771 --> 00:00:56,609
Ahrefs compared the top two hundred domains cited in US ChatGPT answers, in March and September 2026.

8
00:00:56,810 --> 00:01:05,384
Reddit fell from nineteen percent of answers to about two. Wikipedia fell from fourteen percent to about three.

9
00:01:05,584 --> 00:01:15,237
Government and research sites, regulators and hands-on product testers gained. Marketplaces and explainer sites lost ground.

10
00:01:15,438 --> 00:01:24,227
It is US data from one period, so treat it as a clue. Your own category's sources list is the real evidence.

11
00:01:24,427 --> 00:01:33,265
Step one. Write ten buyer questions, the way your buyers really ask. Leave your brand name out.

12
00:01:33,465 --> 00:01:42,111
Run each one in ChatGPT with search on, in a fresh chat. Open the sources and copy every link.

13
00:01:42,311 --> 00:01:50,981
Note who each page names: you, your competitors, or nobody. Then run it all again on another day.

14
00:01:51,182 --> 00:01:56,587
Step two. Sort every source into one of five buckets.

15
00:01:56,787 --> 00:02:05,817
One. Your own website. If it never appears, first check that ChatGPT's search crawler can reach it.

16
00:02:06,018 --> 00:02:16,704
Two. Primary and expert sources. Regulators, research, certification lists, and people who test products hands-on.

17
00:02:16,903 --> 00:02:26,150
Three. Editorial lists, like best sunscreens in India. Many of these are updated every few months.

18
00:02:26,349 --> 00:02:36,171
Four. Communities and video. Reddit, Quora, forums, YouTube, and creators who review your category.

19
00:02:36,371 --> 00:02:46,530
Five. Marketplaces and review sites. Amazon, Flipkart, Nykaa, app stores and software review sites.

20
00:02:46,729 --> 00:02:54,343
Step three. Score each source. One point for every question that lists it.

21
00:02:54,543 --> 00:03:02,061
Plus three if it names a competitor but not you. Plus up to two if you can influence it in ninety days.

22
00:03:02,261 --> 00:03:08,675
Take the top five. That is your outreach and content list for the next quarter.

23
00:03:08,875 --> 00:03:15,409
Step four. Two quick checks. First, your robots file.

24
00:03:15,609 --> 00:03:22,912
OpenAI says sites that block OAI-SearchBot will not be shown in ChatGPT search answers.

25
00:03:23,111 --> 00:03:30,918
It is separate from GPTBot, which is used for training. You can allow one and block the other.

26
00:03:31,117 --> 00:03:38,780
Second. On November tenth, OpenAI announced Businesses in ChatGPT, in beta.

27
00:03:38,979 --> 00:03:46,497
Eligible businesses can claim a profile, verify ownership, and add company details and product feeds.

28
00:03:46,697 --> 00:03:56,135
Indian coverage reports it is free at launch. Business Agents are US-only for now. Check if you can claim yours.

29
00:03:56,335 --> 00:04:00,469
Doing all of this by hand every month takes time.

30
00:04:00,669 --> 00:04:08,403
Jeevan AI shows which competitors AI tools cite instead of you, across every question you track.

31
00:04:08,603 --> 00:04:16,529
Its AEO audit checks your pages, including whether AI crawlers are blocked and whether you are on review sites.

32
00:04:16,729 --> 00:04:22,303
And Gap Finder turns missing citations into a ranked list of gaps to fix.

33
00:04:22,503 --> 00:04:26,637
Try it for your brand at jeevanai.co.in.

34
00:04:26,837 --> 00:04:39,803
Quick recap. Collect your sources. Sort them into five buckets. Pick your top five. Do the two checks. Repeat monthly.

35
00:04:40,003 --> 00:04:46,801
Comment one website that keeps showing up in your category, and we may look at it in a future episode.

36
00:04:47,001 --> 00:04:55,959
Next episode: why AI recommends your competitor, and what to fix first. Subscribe so you do not miss it.
